# Every pull request that changes what a student sees appends one line to the
# patch notes, always at the same place, so N concurrent branches would mean
# N-1 conflicts over independent prose. Union keeps both sides' lines rather
# than conflicting, which is what you want for a list of sentences.
#
# Two things make this safe, and both are load-bearing:
#
#   - The last note in an entry carries a trailing comma. Without one, two
#     appends merge into `'A'` followed by `'C'` with no comma between them --
#     a syntax error, every time.
#   - Nothing depends on the order of notes within an entry; a union merge
#     decides it.
#
# Union never reports a conflict, which for code would be dangerous. Hence one
# path rather than a glob.
src/app/web/patch-notes.ts merge=union
